    "collapsible_tabs_v2_faq": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_v2_1": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What is a GVM upgrade and why does my RAM 2500 6th Gen need one?",
            "content": "<p>GVM stands for Gross Vehicle Mass — the maximum legal weight your vehicle can carry including its own weight, passengers, fuel, accessories, and cargo. Factory GVM ratings are set conservatively and your RAM 2500 6th Gen may not legally carry everything you want to add once you've fitted bull bars, winches, drawers, a canopy, and hitched a heavy trailer.</p><p>A GVM upgrade from ORI is an engineered, certified process that increases your truck's official maximum legal weight rating, giving you more legal payload to work with. It's not just a sticker change — every ORI GVM package includes new suspension components, an engineering certificate, and registration on the Federal compliance database.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": true
          }
        },
        "faq_v2_2": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What GVM stages are available for the RAM 2500 6th Gen?",
            "content": "<p>ORI offers four GVM upgrade stages for the RAM 2500 6th Gen:</p><ul><li><strong>Stage 1</strong> — Entry-level payload boost with Fox 2.0 Performance Series suspension. No wheel or tyre upgrade required. Best for daily drivers and light tourers.</li><li><strong>Stage 2</strong> — Upgraded to Fox 2.5 DSC Performance Elite with adjustable damping. No wheel change required. Best for long-distance corrugated road touring.</li><li><strong>Stage 3</strong> — Heavy hauler configuration with Fox 2.5 PE and ORI 400kg leaf packs. Requires load-rated wheels and tyres. Best for tray and canopy conversions.</li><li><strong>Stage 4</strong> — Maximum capability with Fox 3.0 Internal Bypass race shocks. Requires load-rated wheels and tyres. Australia's highest-spec RAM 2500 6th Gen GVM package.</li></ul><p>Contact our team to discuss which stage suits your exact build.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_v2_3": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "How much payload increase can I expect from a RAM 2500 6th Gen GVM upgrade?",
            "content": "<p>The exact payload increase depends on which stage you select and your specific vehicle's kerb weight. As a general guide, our GVM upgrades are designed to deliver significant payload increases — in some cases well over 50% more than factory ratings, depending on the stage chosen.</p><p>The key numbers to focus on are your starting payload (factory GVM minus kerb weight) and the upgraded GVM rating for your chosen stage. Our specification table on this page outlines the exact figures for each stage. Contact our team for a personalised calculation based on your specific vehicle configuration.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_v2_4": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Is a RAM 2500 6th Gen GVM upgrade legal in all Australian states and territories?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. ORI is a Federally Approved Second Stage Manufacturer (SSM), which means every GVM upgrade we complete is recorded on the official Federal compliance database. This gives your vehicle legal status in all Australian states and territories — not just the state where it was upgraded.</p><p>For Pre-Rego vehicles, your upgrade is processed through the Federal system and applies nationwide from day one. For Post-Rego vehicles, state-based processing applies. Our team will guide you through the exact compliance pathway for your situation during the enquiry process.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_v2_5": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Can I still tow my caravan or trailer after a RAM 2500 6th Gen GVM upgrade?",
            "content": "<p>Yes — all ORI GVM packages for the RAM 2500 6th Gen are designed to retain your vehicle's full braked towing capacity. The GCM (Gross Combined Mass) is also upgraded as part of the package, ensuring your truck, trailer, and all your gear remain fully legal together.</p><p>If you're planning to tow a heavy van or trailer, make sure to mention this when you contact our team. We'll confirm the exact GCM rating for your chosen stage and ensure your complete towing setup is covered.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_v2_6": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What's the difference between a Pre-Rego and Post-Rego GVM upgrade?",
            "content": "<p><strong>Pre-Rego (Federal):</strong> The upgrade is completed before your vehicle is first registered. This is processed through the Federal compliance system and applies in every Australian state from day one. Pre-Rego upgrades generally offer the widest range of options and highest GVM ratings.</p><p><strong>Post-Rego (State-based):</strong> The upgrade is completed after your vehicle is already registered. This is processed through your state's engineering certification system. The process is slightly different state by state, and some limitations may apply depending on your location.</p><p>Our team will advise you on the right pathway based on your vehicle's current registration status during the enquiry process.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_v2_7": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What suspension brands does ORI use in their RAM 2500 6th Gen GVM packages?",
            "content": "<p>Every ORI GVM package uses premium components from two of the world's most respected suspension brands:</p><ul><li><strong>Fox Suspension</strong> — USA-made performance shocks and coilovers. Depending on your stage, you'll receive Fox 2.0 Performance Series, Fox 2.5 Performance Elite DSC (with adjustable damping), or Fox 3.0 Internal Bypass race-spec shocks.</li><li><strong>BDS Suspension</strong> — Heavy-duty control arms engineered for the demands of Australian road conditions under maximum load.</li></ul><p>Combined with ORI's own heavy-duty leaf packs (available in 200kg and 400kg ratings), these components are specifically engineered and tested for the RAM 2500 6th Gen platform.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_v2_8": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Does my insurance still cover me after a GVM upgrade?",
            "content": "<p>Yes — provided your GVM upgrade is properly engineered and certified, your insurance coverage is not voided. Because ORI is a Federally Approved SSM and all our upgrades are recorded on the official Federal database, insurers can verify your upgrade is legitimate and compliant.</p><p>We recommend informing your insurer of the upgrade once it's complete and providing them with your engineering certificate. If you have specific questions about your insurance policy in relation to a GVM upgrade, we recommend speaking with your broker or insurer directly.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        }
      },
